/*
    Espaces-MetaSurface.jsfx-inc  (2026-11-23)

    ====================================== The MetaSurfaces ======================================

    The design : CMGS-Internals, chapter "La MetaSurface d'Espaces (projet)" (its source :
    CMGS-aux/tools/md2odt/D3-MetaSurface-conception.md). A MetaSurface : a rectangle where configurations of the library
    (2 ... MS_MAXC) are placed, each one at a point with a weight ; a brush over it mixes the matrices of the neighbouring
    configurations (an interpolation at constant power, as the Hyper Slider : configurations on a line give exactly its
    effect) into the target matrix of a projector.

    Step 1 (this file, 2026-11-23) : the library MS1 ... MS32 and the views "MetaSurface A" ... "D" in the mode Edit : the
    surface, its band, the configurations placed on it, their zones of influence (a weighted Voronoi diagram : the
    distance to a configuration divided by its weight) ; no sound yet (the mode Play only stops the editing).

    Step 2 (2026-11-23) : the brush, in the mode Play (no sound yet) : a yellow halo (its contour, the contour where its
    energy is half, its centre, the place of the mouse ; held : dashed), its settings on the second line of the pad (Spread,
    Power, Shape, Stretch, Offset, Rotation, Angle ; the brush on the mouse or held), the shares of the configurations under
    it (written next to them) and its coverage of the surface. The shares (ms_Shares) : the brush sampled (8 rings x 24
    rays, weighted by its energy) ; each sample inside the surface : its coordinates among the configurations (ms_Coords :
    barycentric in the Delaunay triangulation of the configurations, ms_Triangulate ; outside their hull, on its nearest
    edge ; configurations on a line : between the two neighbours), each one b -> sin^2(pi b / 2), times the weight of its
    configuration, normalized : on a line, exactly the Hyper Slider. The mouse : the brush follows it inside the surface
    and its band, stays where it is when the mouse goes elsewhere ; Alt + clic (or the cell Brush) : held / attached again ;
    the wheel : Spread (Shift : Power).

    Step 3 (2026-11-23) : the sound (see "The sound" below) : a view in Play drives the projector of its MetaSurface from
    its first start ; a clic on the surface (or the cell of the state) : left, start with a fade-in (Attack : the spread and
    the volume from 0) / stop with a fade-out (Release) ; right, at once ; the halo green while it sounds ; the third line
    of the pad : Volume, Latency (fixed, or for each tenth of the diagonal moved), Attack, Release, the state.

    Step 5 (2026-11-23) : the surface (the cell Aspect : 9 aspects, portraits too ; a quarter turn either way, flipped up -
    down or left - right : its configurations, the brush, its angle with it ; a rectangle or a disk, an ellipse when it is
    not square) ; the trajectories (the fourth line of the pad : the brush on the mouse or on a path ; the path : none, the
    editor Edit A ... D (live : in its view from the top, the zones of the MetaSurface under its points, ed_MsBack) or a
    trajectory T1 ... T128 of the library ; its duration ; Once, Loop, Back and forth ; the speed constant along it or the
    same time between its points ; Simulate : the brush on the path without sound ; Record : the brush on the mouse
    recorded every 50 ms into a trajectory of the library, which becomes the path).

    Then (2026-11-23, the user) : Play / Edit as a bypass (ms_Bypass : back in Play, the sound and the motion go on from
    where they were) ; Pause (cell 22 : the motion and the rotation stopped, the sound going on) ; the cell 18 "Rule" ;
    Loop reverse ; the path placed on the surface (line 5 of the pad : x, y, turn, scale around its centre, ms_TfGet,
    ms_TfFwd, ms_TfInv ; Placement : reset, centre, fit ; the editors show the surface placed under their path, ms_ZonesEd)
    ; the path drawn well visible on all the themes, in Edit too (ms_PathDraw).

    2026-11-24 (the user : the system of the views Space) : the trajectories A ... D (the kinds of the spatial projectors :
    the shapes of Space 3D with their radius, the paths of Edit A ... D, the library T1 ... T128), each one with its
    placement (x, y, turn, scale around its barycentre), blended by the mix along the chain (A B, A B C, A B C D) or by a
    glide (ms_WCur, ms_GlStart : Cmd + clic on A ... D, the mode Glide), with the code of the spatial projectors
    (sp_MkBlend in the plane x, y ; ms_PathLoad, its key ms_PathKey) ; the dynamics (sp_Ease : the curves of Space, their
    modes) ; the placement of the whole path after it. The pad : 6 lines (line 4 : Brush, A, B, C, D, Mix, Glide, Dyn ;
    line 5 : Duration, the mode, Speed, Radius, Simulate, Record, Restart, the counter ; line 6 : x, y, turn, scale,
    Placement, Place). The entries saved before ('msf1', 200 words) : migrated (ms_Migrate ; their path in A).

    2026-11-24 (step 4 of the curves) : the settings (blocks "MetaSurface n keys ..." of the mSL settings : mst_Meta in
    Espaces-Set-Table, staged, taken by ms_Frame : ms_TbTake ; a file dropped on a view : its first block goes into the
    entry it shows, ms_DropTarget) and the exports (Actions : this entry, or all those used, with the curves, the
    trajectories of the library and the paths of the editors they use : ms_Export).

    The library (ms_lib + e * MS_ES, e = 0 ... MS_NLIB - 1, "MS1" ... "MS32") : [ms_eUsed] 1 when it has been used
    (a configuration, a name), [ms_eN] the count of its configurations, [ms_eSet + k] its settings (ms_s... ; those of
    the next steps already there, with their defaults : the format saved stays the same), [ms_eName + k] its name (the
    codes of its characters, 0 at the end), [ms_eCf + 4 i] the configuration i : its number (conflist), its place x, y
    (0 ... 1 : the surface, x to the right, y down), its weight (0.1 ... 10 ; 1 : its zone as the others). ms_seq[e]
    counts its changes (the views draw it again).
    The views (ms_vw + v * MS_VS, v = 0 ... MS_NV - 1) : the entry shown, the mode (0 Edit, 1 Play), the configuration
    selected (-1 : none). The drawing of a view : its background, the band, the zones, the frame of the surface in an
    offscreen image (MS_IMG + v ; the zones : MS_IMGZ + v, one pixel per node of their grid, enlarged with the filtering
    of gfx_blit), drawn again only when the entry, its configurations, the size or the theme change ;
    the configurations (marks, numbers, names, weights) over it at each frame.
    The background : that of the theme (uix_jbg_color, ui-lib-JJ-GUI ; with its shade). The zones : each configuration has its color, a light pastel (its hue from its number : the same configuration has the
    same color everywhere), going to white (light themes) or to black (dark themes) near the frontiers (the relative gap
    between the two nearest distances, over 3 cells at least) ; computed at the nodes of a grid (coarser while a
    configuration is dragged).
    The mouse, mode Edit : right clic on the surface, add a configuration there (the menu of the library of the
    configurations) ; on a configuration, its menu (another configuration, its weight, remove it) ; left drag of a
    configuration : moved ; Alt + vertical drag : its weight ; a clic : selected. The mode Play never moves them.
    The pad : the MetaSurface shown (left : the next one, Shift : the previous one ; right : the menu of the library),
    the mode, the count of configurations, the aspect of the surface, the band, the projector (used from step 3), the
    weight of the configuration selected (a drag), Actions (rename, duplicate, remove).
    Saved with the project : ms_Serialize, record 'msf1' (the last record of @serialize).
    Included in @init after Espaces-ConfEditor (ce_NmCmp, ce_srt), Espaces-Projectors (prv_MenuEnd), mSL_Panes
    part 1 (keepBlockInfos) ; functions only, except the data below.
*/

MS_NLIB = 32;               // the library : MS1 ... MS32
MS_MAXC = 32;               // the configurations of a MetaSurface
MS_NV = 4;                  // the views "MetaSurface A" ... "D"
MS_NS = 64;                 // the settings of a MetaSurface (2026-11-24 : 64 ; 32 until then, record 'msf1')
MS_NMLEN = 32;              // the characters of a name
MS_ES = 240;                // an entry of the library (2026-11-24 : 240 ; 200 until then)
ms_eUsed = 0; ms_eN = 1; ms_eSet = 2; ms_eName = ms_eSet + MS_NS; ms_eCf = ms_eName + MS_NMLEN; // (ms_eCf + 4 * MS_MAXC <= MS_ES)
// the settings (ms_eSet + k) : the surface (aspect : its width / its height ; band : the width of the band around it, in
// heights of the surface ; the projector it drives, 1 ...) ; the brush, the times (steps 2 and 3, see the design)
ms_sAspect = 0; ms_sBand = 1; ms_sProj = 2; ms_sSpread = 3; ms_sPower = 4; ms_sShape = 5; ms_sStretch = 6;
ms_sOffset = 7; ms_sRot = 8; ms_sAngle = 9; ms_sVol = 10; ms_sLat = 11; ms_sLatMode = 12; ms_sAtt = 13; ms_sRel = 14;
ms_sRotMem = 15; // (the rotation before Shift + clic on the cell Rotation set it Off : restored by the next one)
// (step 5, 2026-11-23) the shape of the surface (0 a rectangle, 1 a disk : an ellipse when it is not square) ; the trajectory
// (its source : 0 none, 1 ... 128 the trajectory T1 ... T128 of the library, 129 ... 132 the path of the editor Edit A ... D ;
// its duration, s ; its mode : 0 Once, 1 Loop, 2 Back and forth ; its speed : 0 constant along the path, 1 the same time
// between its points ; the brush : 0 on the mouse, 1 on the path)
ms_sSurf = 16; ms_sTraj = 17; ms_sDur = 18; ms_sLoop = 19; ms_sSpeedM = 20; ms_sPath = 21;
// (2026-11-23, the user) the motion : 3 Loop reverse too ; the path placed on the surface, around its centre : moved
// (ms_sTx : a part of its width, to the right ; ms_sTy : of its height, up), turned (ms_sTa : degrees, clockwise), scaled
// (ms_sTk : 0.1 ... 10 ; 0, in the entries saved before : 1)
ms_sTx = 22; ms_sTy = 23; ms_sTa = 24; ms_sTk = 25;
// (2026-11-24, the user : the system of the views Space) the trajectories A ... D (ms_sTrK + t : their kinds, those of the
// spatial projectors : 0 ... 5 the shapes of Space 3D, SP_KED + e the path of the editor Edit A ... D, SP_KLIB + i the
// trajectory T(i + 1) of the library ; ms_sTraj is no more used : the entries saved before have their path in A), the
// count of the chain of the mix (ms_sTrN : 2 A B, 3 A B C, 4 A B C D), the mix (ms_sMix : 0 ... 1 along the chain), the
// glide (ms_sGlide : its time, 1 ... 300 s ; ms_sGMode 1 : a change of the mix glides), the radius of the shapes
// (ms_sRad), the dynamics (ms_sCurve : the curve, s3d_EaseNames ; ms_sDMode : in, out, in-out, out-in) ; the placement of
// each trajectory (ms_sPl + 4 t : x, a part of the width of the surface, to the right ; y, of its height, up ; its turn,
// degrees clockwise ; its scale, around its barycentre ; then the placement of the whole path, ms_sTx ...)
ms_sTrK = 26; ms_sTrN = 30; ms_sMix = 31; ms_sGlide = 32; ms_sGMode = 33; ms_sRad = 34; ms_sCurve = 35; ms_sDMode = 36;
ms_sPl = 37; // (37 ... 52)
// (2026-11-24, the user) the flips of the trajectories (ms_sFlip, bits : 1 the whole path left - right, 2 up - down ; the
// trajectory t : 2^(2 + 2 t) left - right, 2^(3 + 2 t) up - down ; see ms_FlipBit)
ms_sFlip = 53;
// (2026-11-24, step 3 of the curves) the modulators by a curve (ms_sMod + 3 j, j : 0 the rotation of the brush, 1 the speed
// of the motion, 2 the mix) : the curve + 1 (0 : off), the cycle (0 : the place of the brush on the path ; else a period,
// s), the depth (the rotation and the speed multiplied by 1 + depth x F ; the mix : + depth x F) ; 63 : free
ms_sMod = 54; // (54 ... 62)
ms_lib = make_array(MS_NLIB * MS_ES);
ms_seq = make_array(MS_NLIB);
// (2026-11-24, step 4 of the curves) the blocks MetaSurface of the settings (mst_Meta, Espaces-Set-Table) : the work area
// (the values as an entry ; the keys given : the settings, the name, the zones ; the entries read), the staging (taken by
// ms_Frame, ms_TbTake)
MST_TF = MS_NS + 2;
mst_tw = make_array(MS_NLIB * MS_ES); mst_twF = make_array(MS_NLIB * MST_TF); mst_twOn = make_array(MS_NLIB);
mst_ts = make_array(MS_NLIB * MS_ES); mst_tsF = make_array(MS_NLIB * MST_TF); mst_tq = make_array(MS_NLIB);
// the views
MS_VS = 16; ms_vE = 0; ms_vMode = 1; ms_vSel = 2;
// (step 2) Edit : the brush shown (held, moved by its cross and its shape) ; the brush saved (ms_bx, ms_by, ms_att ; ms_vInit 1)
ms_vBrush = 3; ms_vBx = 4; ms_vBy = 5; ms_vAtt = 6; ms_vInit = 7;
ms_vw = make_array(MS_NV * MS_VS);
// (2026-11-24) the place of each view (its module) and the frame where it was drawn : a file dropped on it (ms_DropTarget)
ms_mr = make_array(4 * MS_NV); ms_mf = make_array(MS_NV);
i__k = 0; loop(MS_NV, ms_mf[i__k] = -10; i__k += 1;);
// (not saved) the offscreen images and the keys of their drawings (entry, seq, w, h, background, cell size, aspect, band)
MS_IMG = 80;                // MS_IMG ... MS_IMG + 3
i__k = 0; loop(MS_NV, ui_reserve_image(MS_IMG + i__k); i__k += 1;);
MS_IKS = 8;
ms_ik = make_array(MS_NV * MS_IKS);
// the surface in each view (screen pixels : its rectangle, the band around it) ; the mouse (the drag, its view seen)
ms_gx = make_array(MS_NV); ms_gy = make_array(MS_NV); ms_gw = make_array(MS_NV); ms_gh = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_gb = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_md = make_array(MS_NV); ms_seen = make_array(MS_NV); ms_hov = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_dmv = ms_dc = ms_mx0 = ms_my0 = ms_dalt = ms_w0 = 0;
ms_drag = 0;                // a configuration dragged (the zones drawn coarser)
// the zones : a small image (one pixel per node of their grid, MS_ZMAX x MS_ZMAX at most), enlarged (see ms_Render)
MS_IMGZ = 84;               // MS_IMGZ ... MS_IMGZ + 3
i__k = 0; loop(MS_NV, ui_reserve_image(MS_IMGZ + i__k); i__k += 1;);
MS_ZMAX = 1024;
// the menus of the configurations : the number of each item
ms_map = make_array(4200);
ms_pend = 0;                // a rename asked (view + 1, see ms_Prompted)
MS_ASP = "1:1|4:3|3:2|16:9|2:1|3:4|2:3|9:16|1:2"; // (2026-11-23 : the portraits too, see ms_Turn)
MS_NASP = 9;

// (Step 2, 2026-11-23) The brush of each view (not saved) : its point (ms_bx, ms_by : the place of the mouse, in the surface,
// 0 ... 1 ; in the band : beyond), attached to the mouse or held (ms_att : 1 the brush follows the mouse inside the surface
// and its band ; Alt + clic : held / attached again ; the mouse elsewhere : it stays), the phase of its rotation (ms_ph, in
// turns ; ms_lt : the time of the last update), the shares of the configurations (ms_sh + v * MS_MAXC, sum 1), the
// coverage (ms_cov : the part of its energy inside the surface)
ms_bx = make_array(MS_NV); ms_by = make_array(MS_NV); ms_att = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_ph = make_array(MS_NV); ms_lt = make_array(MS_NV); ms_cov = make_array(MS_NV);
i__k = 0; loop(MS_NV, ms_bx[i__k] = ms_by[i__k] = 0.5; ms_att[i__k] = 1; i__k += 1;);
// the drag of the brush (ms_bd : 1 its cross, 2 its shape ; ms_bmv : moved ; ms_gvx, ms_gvy : the centre from the mouse)
ms_bd = make_array(MS_NV); ms_bmv = ms_gvx = ms_gvy = 0;
ms_bq = make_array(2 * 49); // (the points of a contour of the brush, ms_DrawBrush)
// (2026-11-23) the placement of the path dragged (ms_qk : 0 none, 1 moved, 2 scaled, 3 turned, 4 turned and scaled ; the
// button, the press, the placement then ; its centre on the screen)
ms_qk = make_array(MS_NV); ms_qb = ms_qx0 = ms_qy0 = ms_qtx = ms_qty = ms_qta = ms_qtk = ms_qcx = ms_qcy = 0;
ms_hlt = 0;                 // (a light theme : the colors of the halo, ms_HaloSet)
ms_sh = make_array(MS_NV * MS_MAXC);
MS_RINGS = 8; MS_RAYS = 24;  // the samples of the brush : rings x rays
// The interpolation (see ms_Coords) : the Delaunay triangulation of the configurations of the entry shown by each view (kept
// until the entry or its configurations change : ms_tkE, ms_tkS), its triangles (ms_tri : 3 indices each, MS_TMAX at most),
// the edges of its hull (ms_hul : 2 indices each) ; configurations on a line (ms_lin 1 ; or two only) : their order along it
// (ms_ord, their abscissas ms_ta, from the configuration ms_l0 in the direction ms_ldx, ms_ldy)
MS_TMAX = 2 * MS_MAXC;
ms_tri = make_array(MS_NV * MS_TMAX * 3); ms_ntri = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_hul = make_array(MS_NV * MS_MAXC * 2 * 2); ms_nhul = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_ord = make_array(MS_NV * MS_MAXC); ms_ta = make_array(MS_NV * MS_MAXC);
ms_lin = make_array(MS_NV); ms_l0 = make_array(MS_NV); ms_ldx = make_array(MS_NV); ms_ldy = make_array(MS_NV);
ms_tkE = make_array(MS_NV); ms_tkS = make_array(MS_NV);
i__k = 0; loop(MS_NV, ms_tkE[i__k] = -1; i__k += 1;);
// the work of the triangulation (Bowyer-Watson) : the points (the configurations, then the 3 of the super triangle), the
// triangles (a, b, c, the centre and the square of the radius of their circumcircle, alive), the edges of the cavity
MS_WTN = 4 * MS_MAXC + 16;
ms_X = make_array(MS_MAXC + 3); ms_Y = make_array(MS_MAXC + 3);
ms_wt = make_array(MS_WTN * 7); ms_ed = make_array(MS_WTN * 3 * 2);

// The entry e, the configuration i of the entry e
function ms_E(e) ( ms_lib + max(0, min(MS_NLIB - 1, e|0)) * MS_ES; );
function ms_C(e, i) ( ms_E(e) + ms_eCf + 4 * i; );
// (the values through functions : EEL2 does not index the result of a function)
function ms_N(e) local(b) ( b = ms_E(e); b[ms_eN]; );
function ms_Cv(e, i, k) local(p) ( p = ms_C(e, i); p[k]; );
function ms_CSet(e, i, k, x) local(p) ( p = ms_C(e, i); p[k] = x; ms_seq[e] += 1; );
function ms_VGet(v, k) local(p) ( p = ms_vw + v * MS_VS; p[k]; );
function ms_VSet(v, k, x) local(p) ( p = ms_vw + v * MS_VS; p[k] = x; );
// An angle in degrees brought into [0, 360) (EEL2 : % works on integers, and not as needed on negative numbers)
function ms_Wrap360(d) ( d - 360 * floor(d / 360); );
// The settings of the entry e (the value k)
function ms_S(e, k) local(b) ( b = ms_E(e); b[ms_eSet + k]; );
function ms_SSet(e, k, x) local(b) ( b = ms_E(e); b[ms_eSet + k] = x; b[ms_eUsed] = 1; );
// (step 5) The point u, v (0 ... 1 : the rectangle of the surface) inside the surface of the entry e enlarged by m (in
// heights : 0 the surface, the band : surface and band) : a rectangle, or a disk (an ellipse : in u, v the circle of
// radius 0.5 around 0.5, 0.5)
function ms_InUV(e, u, v, m) local(a)
(
    a = max(0.5, min(4, ms_S(e, ms_sAspect)));
    ms_S(e, ms_sSurf) ? (sqr((u - 0.5) * a / (a / 2 + m)) + sqr((v - 0.5) / (0.5 + m)) <= 1) :
        ((u >= -m / a) && (u <= 1 + m / a) && (v >= -m) && (v <= 1 + m));
);
// the point u, v brought inside the surface enlarged by m : ms_cu, ms_cv
function ms_Clamp(e, u, v, m) local(a, x, y, r)
(
    a = max(0.5, min(4, ms_S(e, ms_sAspect)));
    ms_S(e, ms_sSurf) ? (
        x = (u - 0.5) * a / (a / 2 + m); y = (v - 0.5) / (0.5 + m); r = sqrt(x * x + y * y);
        (r > 1) ? (x /= r; y /= r;);
        ms_cu = 0.5 + x * (a / 2 + m) / a; ms_cv = 0.5 + y * (0.5 + m);
    ) : (
        ms_cu = max(-m / a, min(1 + m / a, u)); ms_cv = max(-m, min(1 + m, v));
    );
);
// A filled ellipse (screen pixels : its centre, its half axes), a line of pixels at a time ; its contour (n segments)
// (the color : gfx_r, gfx_g, gfx_b ; the pixels of the edges partly covered : their alpha, 2026-11-23)
function ms_FillEll(cx, cy, rx, ry) local(y, d, w, xl, xr, il, ir, r, g, b)
(
    r = gfx_r; g = gfx_g; b = gfx_b;
    y = floor(cy - ry);
    loop(ceil(2 * ry) + 2,
        d = (y + 0.5 - cy) / max(1, ry);
        (abs(d) < 1) ? (
            w = rx * sqrt(1 - d * d); xl = cx - w; xr = cx + w; il = floor(xl); ir = floor(xr);
            gfx_set(r, g, b, 1);
            (ir > il + 1) ? gfx_rect(il + 1, y, ir - il - 1, 1);
            gfx_set(r, g, b, 1 - (xl - il)); gfx_rect(il, y, 1, 1);
            (ir > il) ? (gfx_set(r, g, b, xr - ir); gfx_rect(ir, y, 1, 1););
        );
        y += 1;
    );
    gfx_set(r, g, b, 1);
);
// The rectangle sx, sy, sw, sh painted outside the ellipse inscribed in it (r, g, b ; the pixels of the edge partly outside :
// their alpha) : the zones of a disk cut exactly, not at the resolution of their grid (2026-11-23, the user : crenels)
function ms_MaskEll(sx, sy, sw, sh, r, g, b) local(y, cx, cy, rx, ry, d, w, xl, xr, il, ir)
(
    cx = sx + sw / 2; cy = sy + sh / 2; rx = sw / 2; ry = sh / 2;
    y = sy;
    loop(sh,
        d = (y + 0.5 - cy) / max(1, ry);
        gfx_set(r, g, b, 1);
        (abs(d) >= 1) ? gfx_rect(sx, y, sw, 1) : (
            w = rx * sqrt(1 - d * d); xl = cx - w; xr = cx + w; il = floor(xl); ir = floor(xr);
            (il > sx) ? gfx_rect(sx, y, il - sx, 1);
            (ir + 1 < sx + sw) ? gfx_rect(ir + 1, y, sx + sw - ir - 1, 1);
            gfx_set(r, g, b, xl - il); gfx_rect(il, y, 1, 1);
            gfx_set(r, g, b, 1 - (xr - ir)); gfx_rect(ir, y, 1, 1);
        );
        y += 1;
    );
);
function ms_LineEll(cx, cy, rx, ry) local(k, x0, y0, x1, y1)
(
    x0 = cx + rx; y0 = cy;
    k = 1;
    loop(96, x1 = cx + rx * cos(2 * $pi * k / 96); y1 = cy + ry * sin(2 * $pi * k / 96); gfx_line(x0, y0, x1, y1, 1); x0 = x1; y0 = y1; k += 1;);
);
// The surface of the entry e turned (step 5, 2026-11-23 ; kind : 1 a quarter turn clockwise, 2 counterclockwise, 3 flipped
// up - down, 4 left - right) : its configurations, its aspect (a quarter turn : inverted), the brushes of the views that show
// it, the angle of the brush (and the direction of its rotation when flipped)
function ms_Turn(e, kind) local(i, p, u, v, b, vw)
(
    i = 0;
    loop(ms_N(e),
        p = ms_C(e, i); u = p[1]; v = p[2];
        (kind === 1) ? (p[1] = 1 - v; p[2] = u;) : (kind === 2) ? (p[1] = v; p[2] = 1 - u;) :
        (kind === 3) ? (p[2] = 1 - v) : (p[1] = 1 - u);
        i += 1;
    );
    b = 0;
    loop(MS_NV,
        vw = ms_vw + b * MS_VS;
        (vw[ms_vE] === e) ? (
            u = ms_bx[b]; v = ms_by[b];
            (kind === 1) ? (ms_bx[b] = 1 - v; ms_by[b] = u;) : (kind === 2) ? (ms_bx[b] = v; ms_by[b] = 1 - u;) :
            (kind === 3) ? (ms_by[b] = 1 - v) : (ms_bx[b] = 1 - u);
        );
        b += 1;
    );
    ((kind === 1) || (kind === 2)) ? ms_SSet(e, ms_sAspect, 1 / max(0.5, min(4, ms_S(e, ms_sAspect))));
    ms_SSet(e, ms_sAngle, ms_Wrap360((kind === 1) ? ms_S(e, ms_sAngle) + 90 : (kind === 2) ? ms_S(e, ms_sAngle) - 90 :
        (kind === 3) ? 180 - ms_S(e, ms_sAngle) : -ms_S(e, ms_sAngle)));
    (kind >= 3) ? (ms_SSet(e, ms_sRot, -ms_S(e, ms_sRot)); ms_SSet(e, ms_sRotMem, -ms_S(e, ms_sRotMem)););
    ms_seq[e] += 1;
);

function ms_Aspect(k) ( (k === 0) ? 1 : (k === 1) ? 4 / 3 : (k === 2) ? 1.5 : (k === 3) ? 16 / 9 : (k === 4) ? 2 :
    (k === 5) ? 3 / 4 : (k === 6) ? 2 / 3 : (k === 7) ? 9 / 16 : 0.5; );
// the nearest of the aspects of the list
function ms_AspK(a) local(k, m, d, r) ( r = 0; m = 10^9; k = 0; loop(MS_NASP, d = abs(log(max(0.01, a) / ms_Aspect(k))); (d < m) ? (m = d; r = k;); k += 1;); r; );

// The settings of the entry e at their defaults
function ms_SetDefaults(e) local(b, s)
(
    b = ms_E(e); s = b + ms_eSet;
    memset(s, 0, MS_NS);
    s[ms_sAspect] = 1.5; s[ms_sBand] = 0.08; s[ms_sProj] = 1;
    s[ms_sSpread] = 0.15; s[ms_sPower] = 0; s[ms_sShape] = 0; s[ms_sStretch] = 1; s[ms_sOffset] = 0;
    s[ms_sRot] = 0; s[ms_sAngle] = 0; s[ms_sVol] = 0; s[ms_sLat] = 80; s[ms_sLatMode] = 0; s[ms_sAtt] = 2; s[ms_sRel] = 4;
    s[ms_sSurf] = 0; s[ms_sTraj] = 0; s[ms_sDur] = 20; s[ms_sLoop] = 1; s[ms_sSpeedM] = 0; s[ms_sPath] = 0;
    s[ms_sTx] = s[ms_sTy] = s[ms_sTa] = 0; s[ms_sTk] = 1;
    // (2026-11-24) the trajectories A ... D : Circle, Square, Star, Spiral ; the chain A B, the mix 0 (A) ; glide 10 s, no
    // mode Glide ; radius 0.6 ; Linear ; no placement (scale 1)
    s[ms_sTrK] = 1; s[ms_sTrK + 1] = 2; s[ms_sTrK + 2] = 3; s[ms_sTrK + 3] = 4;
    s[ms_sTrN] = 2; s[ms_sMix] = 0; s[ms_sGlide] = 10; s[ms_sGMode] = 0; s[ms_sRad] = 0.6; s[ms_sCurve] = 0; s[ms_sDMode] = 0;
    s[ms_sPl + 3] = s[ms_sPl + 7] = s[ms_sPl + 11] = s[ms_sPl + 15] = 1;
    // (2026-11-24, step 3) the modulators : off, the cycle Path, the depth 1
    s[ms_sMod + 2] = s[ms_sMod + 5] = s[ms_sMod + 8] = 1;
);
// The entry e emptied (no configuration, no name, the defaults)
function ms_Clear(e) local(b)
(
    b = ms_E(e);
    memset(b, 0, MS_ES);
    ms_SetDefaults(e);
    ms_seq[e] += 1;
);
function ms_Init() local(e, v, vw)
(
    e = 0; loop(MS_NLIB, ms_Clear(e); e += 1;);
    v = 0; loop(MS_NV, vw = ms_vw + v * MS_VS; memset(vw, 0, MS_VS); vw[ms_vE] = v; vw[ms_vSel] = -1; v += 1;);
);
ms_Init();

// The name of the entry e into s (empty : none) ; returns s
function ms_Name(e, s) local(b, k, c)
(
    strcpy(s, "");
    b = ms_E(e) + ms_eName; k = 0;
    while ((k < MS_NMLEN) && ((c = b[k]) > 0)) (sprintf(#ms_ch, "%c", c); strcat(s, #ms_ch); k += 1;);
    s;
);
// its new name (the quotes become ', | becomes / : as cf_NewW)
function ms_SetName(e, s) local(b, k, l, c)
(
    b = ms_E(e) + ms_eName; memset(b, 0, MS_NMLEN);
    l = min(MS_NMLEN - 1, strlen(s)); k = 0;
    loop(l, c = str_getchar(s, k, 'cu'); b[k] = (c === '"') ? 39 : (c === '|') ? '/' : (c < 32) ? 32 : c; k += 1;);
    b = ms_E(e); (l > 0) ? b[ms_eUsed] = 1;
    ms_seq[e] += 1;
);
// "MS3", "MS3 : name" into s ; returns s
function ms_Label(e, s)
(
    sprintf(s, "MS%d", e + 1);
    (strlen(ms_Name(e, #ms_nm)) > 0) ? (strcat(s, " : "); strcat(s, #ms_nm););
    s;
);

// A configuration c placed at u, v (0 ... 1) on the entry e, weight 1 : its index (-1 : full)
function ms_Add(e, c, u, v) local(b, p, i)
(
    b = ms_E(e); i = -1;
    (b[ms_eN] < MS_MAXC) ? (
        i = b[ms_eN]; p = ms_C(e, i);
        p[0] = c; p[1] = max(0, min(1, u)); p[2] = max(0, min(1, v)); p[3] = 1;
        b[ms_eN] += 1; b[ms_eUsed] = 1;
        ms_seq[e] += 1;
    );
    i;
);
// The configuration i of the entry e removed (the following ones take its place)
function ms_Del(e, i) local(b, n)
(
    b = ms_E(e); n = b[ms_eN];
    ((i >= 0) && (i < n)) ? (
        (i < n - 1) ? memcpy(ms_C(e, i), ms_C(e, i + 1), 4 * (n - 1 - i));
        memset(ms_C(e, n - 1), 0, 4);
        b[ms_eN] = n - 1;
        ms_seq[e] += 1;
    );
);

// The colors of the configuration c (ms_pr, ms_pg, ms_pb : its pastel ; ms_kr, ms_kg, ms_kb : its mark), on a light
// background (lt 1) or a dark one
function ms_Colors(c, lt) local(h, q)
(
    h = (c * 137.508) % 360;
    q = hsv_to_prgb(h, lt ? 0.30 : 0.42, lt ? 0.98 : 0.74);
    ms_pr = ((q >> 16) & 255) / 255; ms_pg = ((q >> 8) & 255) / 255; ms_pb = (q & 255) / 255;
    q = hsv_to_prgb(h, lt ? 0.78 : 0.62, lt ? 0.78 : 0.98);
    ms_kr = ((q >> 16) & 255) / 255; ms_kg = ((q >> 8) & 255) / 255; ms_kb = (q & 255) / 255;
);

// The surface of the view v in the rectangle x, y, w, h (screen pixels) : ms_gx[v] ... (its rectangle), ms_gb[v] (the band)
function ms_Geo(v, e, x, y, w, h) local(s, a, bd, hs)
(
    s = ms_E(e) + ms_eSet;
    a = max(0.5, min(4, s[ms_sAspect])); bd = max(0, min(0.5, s[ms_sBand]));
    hs = max(8, min(h / (1 + 2 * bd), w / (a + 2 * bd)));
    ms_gw[v] = floor(a * hs); ms_gh[v] = floor(hs); ms_gb[v] = floor(bd * hs);
    ms_gx[v] = floor(x + (w - ms_gw[v]) / 2); ms_gy[v] = floor(y + (h - ms_gh[v]) / 2);
);

// The configurations of the entry e brought inside its surface (a disk : those outside, onto its edge)
function ms_ClampAll(e) local(i, p)
(
    i = 0; loop(ms_N(e), p = ms_C(e, i); ms_Clamp(e, p[1], p[2], 0); p[1] = ms_cu; p[2] = ms_cv; i += 1;);
);

// The color of the point u, v (0 ... 1) of the surface of the entry e (aspect a ; n configurations ; edge : the color of
// the frontiers) : ms_r, ms_g, ms_b
function ms_NodeColor(e, n, a, u, v, lt, er, eg, eb) local(i, p, d, d1, d2, i1, c1, t, f)
(
    // the nearest configuration (d1), then the nearest one of another number (d2 : the same configuration placed twice,
    // near each other, makes one zone, no frontier between them ; 2026-11-23, the user)
    d1 = d2 = 10^9; i1 = -1;
    i = 0;
    loop(n,
        p = ms_C(e, i);
        d = sqrt(sqr((u - p[1]) * a) + sqr(v - p[2])) / max(0.1, p[3]);
        (d < d1) ? (d1 = d; i1 = i;);
        i += 1;
    );
    (i1 >= 0) ? (
        c1 = ms_Cv(e, i1, 0);
        i = 0;
        loop(n,
            p = ms_C(e, i);
            (p[0] !== c1) ? (d = sqrt(sqr((u - p[1]) * a) + sqr(v - p[2])) / max(0.1, p[3]); (d < d2) ? d2 = d;);
            i += 1;
        );
    );
    (i1 < 0) ? (
        ms_r = er; ms_g = eg; ms_b = eb;
    ) : (
        ms_Colors(ms_Cv(e, i1, 0), lt);
        // the gap between the two nearest distances : 0 on a frontier ; the gradient over 22 % of their sum, but at least
        // ms_gmin (about 3 cells of the grid : two configurations close to each other, their frontier stays smooth, not
        // in steps ; 2026-11-23, the user) ; one configuration : no frontier
        t = (d2 < 10^8) ? (d2 - d1) / max(ms_gmin, 0.22 * (d2 + d1)) : 1; // (no other configuration : no frontier)
        f = max(0, min(1, t)); f = f * f * (3 - 2 * f);
        ms_r = er + (ms_pr - er) * f; ms_g = eg + (ms_pg - eg) * f; ms_b = eb + (ms_pb - eb) * f;
    );
);

// The zones of the entry e into the image img, one pixel per node of a grid nx x ny (enlarged by gfx_blit) ; lt : a light
// background ; er, eg, eb : the color of the frontiers ; orr, og, ob : that of the points outside a disk (step 5)
// (the same, flipped : fl 1 left - right, 2 up - down : the backdrop of an editor, see ms_EdBack ; fl 4 : a disk not masked,
// the zones computed on the whole rectangle : the view cuts them exactly, ms_MaskEll)
function ms_ZonesF(e, img, nx, ny, lt, er, eg, eb, orr, og, ob, fl) local(n, a, i, j, u, v, dk)
(
    n = ms_N(e); a = max(0.5, min(4, ms_S(e, ms_sAspect))); dk = ms_S(e, ms_sSurf);
    gfx_setimgdim(img, nx + 1, ny + 1);
    gfx_dest = img;
    j = 0;
    loop(ny + 1,
        i = 0;
        loop(nx + 1,
            u = (fl & 1) ? 1 - i / nx : i / nx; v = (fl & 2) ? 1 - j / ny : j / ny;
            (dk && !(fl & 4) && !ms_InUV(e, u, v, 0)) ? (ms_r = orr; ms_g = og; ms_b = ob;) : ms_NodeColor(e, n, a, u, v, lt, er, eg, eb);
            gfx_x = i; gfx_y = j; gfx_setpixel(ms_r, ms_g, ms_b);
            i += 1;
        );
        j += 1;
    );
);
function ms_Zones(e, img, nx, ny, lt, er, eg, eb, orr, og, ob) local(n, a, i, j, u, v, dk)
(
    ms_ZonesF(e, img, nx, ny, lt, er, eg, eb, orr, og, ob, 0);
);
// The drawing of the view v (background, band, zones, frame) into its image, w x h pixels ; cs : the size of the cells
function ms_Render(v, e, w, h, cs) local(od, b, n, a, lt, er, eg, eb, sx, sy, sw, sh, bd, nx, ny, i, j, t, dk, br, bgc, bb)
(
    od = gfx_dest;
    gfx_setimgdim(MS_IMG + v, w, h);
    gfx_dest = MS_IMG + v;
    gfx_mode = 0;
    b = ms_E(e); n = b[ms_eN]; a = max(0.5, min(4, b[ms_eSet + ms_sAspect]));
    lt = (0.299 * ms_bgr + 0.587 * ms_bgg + 0.114 * ms_bgb) > 0.5;
    er = eg = eb = lt ? 1 : 0;
    gfx_set(ms_bgr, ms_bgg, ms_bgb, 1);
    gfx_rect(0, 0, w, h);
    // (the surface, in the image)
    sx = ms_gx[v] - ms_vx; sy = ms_gy[v] - ms_vy; sw = ms_gw[v]; sh = ms_gh[v]; bd = ms_gb[v];
    // the band : a little darker (light themes) or lighter ; around a disk, a ring (step 5)
    dk = ms_S(e, ms_sSurf);
    t = (bd > 0) ? (lt ? -0.06 : 0.06) : 0;
    br = ms_bgr + t; bgc = ms_bgg + t; bb = ms_bgb + t;
    (bd > 0) ? (
        gfx_set(br, bgc, bb, 1);
        dk ? ms_FillEll(sx + sw / 2, sy + sh / 2, sw / 2 + bd, sh / 2 + bd) : gfx_rect(sx - bd, sy - bd, sw + 2 * bd, sh + 2 * bd);
    );
    // the zones : one pixel per node of a grid (every cs pixels) in a small image (MS_IMGZ + v), enlarged onto the surface
    // by gfx_blit, whose filtering (bilinear) gives continuous gradients (2026-11-23 : the cells drawn by gfx_gradrect from
    // three of their corners made steps along the oblique frontiers)
    nx = min(MS_ZMAX, max(1, ceil(sw / cs))); ny = min(MS_ZMAX, max(1, ceil(sh / cs)));
    ms_gmin = 3 * max(ms_csf, sw / MS_ZMAX) / max(1, sh); // (the narrowest gradient of a frontier : 3 fine cells, in
                                                          // heights of the surface ; the same during a drag)
    ms_ZonesF(e, MS_IMGZ + v, nx, ny, lt, er, eg, eb, br, bgc, bb, 4);
    gfx_dest = MS_IMG + v;
    gfx_a = 1; gfx_mode = 2; // (the alpha of the small image ignored ; its filtering kept)
    gfx_blit(MS_IMGZ + v, 1, 0, 0.5, 0.5, nx, ny, sx, sy, sw, sh);
    gfx_mode = 0;
    dk ? ms_MaskEll(sx, sy, sw, sh, br, bgc, bb); // (a disk : cut exactly)
    // the frame of the surface
    t = lt ? 0.35 : 0.7;
    gfx_set(t, t, t, 0.8);
    dk ? ms_LineEll(sx + sw / 2 - 0.5, sy + sh / 2 - 0.5, sw / 2, sh / 2) : (
        gfx_line(sx, sy, sx + sw - 1, sy); gfx_line(sx + sw - 1, sy, sx + sw - 1, sy + sh - 1);
        gfx_line(sx + sw - 1, sy + sh - 1, sx, sy + sh - 1); gfx_line(sx, sy + sh - 1, sx, sy);
    );
    gfx_dest = od;
);

// ====== Step 2 : the brush, the shares

// The brush of the view v is shown (Play ; Edit : the cell Brush) ; held (shown, not following the mouse : Edit always)
function ms_Shown(v) local(vw) ( vw = ms_vw + v * MS_VS; vw[ms_vMode] || vw[ms_vBrush]; );
function ms_Held(v) local(vw, b) ( vw = ms_vw + v * MS_VS; b = ms_lib + vw[ms_vE] * MS_ES; ms_Shown(v) && (!vw[ms_vMode] || !ms_att[v] || b[ms_eSet + ms_sPath]); );

// The contour of the brush in the direction phi (radians), for its shape S (0 circle, 1 square, 2 cross ; between them, the
// mixture) : its distance from the centre (the circle : 1 ; the square : its corners at sqrt(2))
function ms_Rho(phi, S) local(c, sa, q, x, t1, t2, w)
(
    c = abs(cos(phi)); sa = abs(sin(phi));
    q = 1 / max(c, sa); // (the square)
    (S <= 1) ? (
        1 + (q - 1) * max(0, S);
    ) : (
        // the cross : two arms of half width w ; the ray leaves the arm along x at t1, the arm along y at t2
        w = 0.35;
        t1 = min((c > 0.000001) ? 1 / c : 10^6, (sa > 0.000001) ? w / sa : 10^6);
        t2 = min((c > 0.000001) ? w / c : 10^6, (sa > 0.000001) ? 1 / sa : 10^6);
        x = max(t1, t2);
        q + (x - q) * min(1, S - 1);
    );
);
// The energy of the brush at the radius r (0 its centre ... 1 its edge) for the power P (-1 ... 1) : (1 - r)^(8^P) ; 0 : a
// cone, -1 : nearly the same everywhere, 1 : near the centre
function ms_Prof(r, P) ( (r >= 1) ? 0 : (1 - r) ^ (8 ^ max(-1, min(1, P))); );

// The circumcircle of the work triangle k (its points a, b, c) : the centre, the square of the radius ; aligned points : a
// circle that contains everything (the triangle goes at the next point)
function ms_Circ(k) local(t, a, b, c, ax, ay, bx, by, cx, cy, d, a2, b2, c2)
(
    t = ms_wt + 7 * k; a = t[0]; b = t[1]; c = t[2];
    ax = ms_X[a]; ay = ms_Y[a]; bx = ms_X[b]; by = ms_Y[b]; cx = ms_X[c]; cy = ms_Y[c];
    d = 2 * (ax * (by - cy) + bx * (cy - ay) + cx * (ay - by));
    (abs(d) < 0.000000000001) ? (
        t[3] = t[4] = 0; t[5] = 10^30;
    ) : (
        a2 = ax * ax + ay * ay; b2 = bx * bx + by * by; c2 = cx * cx + cy * cy;
        t[3] = (a2 * (by - cy) + b2 * (cy - ay) + c2 * (ay - by)) / d;
        t[4] = (a2 * (cx - bx) + b2 * (ax - cx) + c2 * (bx - ax)) / d;
        t[5] = sqr(ax - t[3]) + sqr(ay - t[4]);
    );
    t[6] = 1;
